{
  "id": "recall-bias",
  "term": "recall bias",
  "definition": "Recall bias is a systematic difference between what people later remember and what they originally reported or experienced. In psychology and health research, it refers to memory distortion that can make past symptoms, quality of life, or exposures seem better, worse, or different than they were.",
  "field": "cognition",
